    <statement><p>Find a vector function that represents the curve of intersection of 
the paraboloid <m>z = 6 x^2 + 4 y^2</m> and the cylinder
<m>y = 4 x^2</m>.  Use the variable t for the parameter.</p>
<p><m>\mathbf r(t) = \langle t,</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/><m>\rangle</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4tt</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6tt+64t^{4}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
